<!--Post: 2357--><!--Time: 1103570477-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2357"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ashdana<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ashdana<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 20, 2004 - 11:21 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->What if the &#34;fact&#34; that BTK built and operated a HAM radio is completely false...but he threw it in there to point us to something else?  <BR> <BR>I&#39;m wondering about the movie &#34;Frequency&#34; from 2000, a murder mystery/time travel thriller. Here&#39;s a brief description of the plot, which centered heavily around a HAM radio and a serial killer who is terrorizing women: <BR> <BR>Quote: <BR>-------------------------------------------------- ------------------------------ <BR>John Sullivan is a New York City homicide officer who is traumatized for 30 years following the death of his father, Frank. After finding Frank&#39;s HAM radio, John begins talking to Frank, 30 years into the future. Together, they change the past but have to find a way to stop a serial killer from murdering John&#39;s mom/Frank&#39;s wife with a 30 year gap.  <BR>-------------------------------------------------- ------------------------------ <BR> <BR>1. In “Frequency,” the plot jumps forward and backward in time over 30 years...from 1969 to 1999. Sounds like the 30-year gap between 1974 and 2004, doesn&#39;t it?  <BR> <BR>2. The serial killer has a nickname: “The Nightingale Strangler” I believe. <BR> <BR>3. He targets and murders young women; I think the number killed was close to eight.  <BR> <BR>4. The killer &#40;who is found to be a detective&#41; goes dormant and in the part of the movie that takes place in 1999, has been laying low for years. <BR> <BR>What if BTK saw this movie, enjoyed the serial killer cop aspect of it, was struck by some similarities to himself, and is paying homage in some twisted way by painting himself as a HAM radio operator? Or maybe there is something in that movie that would provide a legitimate clue to his identity and he threw the HAM radio references in just to see if anyone would figure it out? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2357-->
<!--Post: 2525--><!--Time: 1103758303-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2525"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iq<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iq<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 22, 2004 - 3:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->maybe he does still operate a ham radio. <BR><a href="http://www.boeingradioclub.org/members.htm" target=_top>http://www.boeingradioclub.org/members.htm</a> <BR> <BR>maybe, maybe not... <BR> <BR>-iq <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2525-->
<!--Post: 2661--><!--Time: 1103891041-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2661"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 24, 2004 - 4:24 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I think it was known about the ham radio  he mentioned well before that movie came out...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2661-->
<!--Post: 2799--><!--Time: 1104156078-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2799"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ashdana<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ashdana<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 27, 2004 - 6:01 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hi Vdubguy, <BR> <BR>Thanks for the response. Do you read somewhere that the &#34;facts&#34; about BTK were gleaned from the older letters? I may be mistaken, but I thought that most of the facts were from the 2004 communiques. Any additional info you can provide would be greatly appreciated.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2799-->
<!--Post: 2832--><!--Time: 1104175249-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2832"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 27, 2004 - 11:20 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I could be wrong on that Ashdana...but i thought i had read that that was from an earlier communique. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2832-->
<!--Post: 2836--><!--Time: 1104175947-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2836"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:jsk@jvlnet.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 27, 2004 - 11:32 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Do you happen to live in that area Ashdana? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2836-->
<!--Post: 2839--><!--Time: 1104178052-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2839"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Secret_squirrel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Secret_squirrel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 27, 2004 - 12:07 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->According to Jeff&#39;s ameteur radio page, &#34;You can always spot a hams house.  The antenna is bigger than the house.&#34; <BR> <BR>Just an FYI for those of you in the Wichita area.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2839-->
<!--Post: 2960--><!--Time: 1104340042-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2960"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ashdana<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ashdana<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 9:07 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->No, Vdubguy, I live near Washington, DC.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2960-->
<!--Post: 3024--><!--Time: 1104374977-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3024"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:jsk@jvlnet.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 6:49 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Secret...except for my house...youd NEVEr know i was a ham!<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3024-->
<!--Post: 3052--><!--Time: 1104385372-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3052"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Secret_squirrel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Secret_squirrel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 9:42 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I imagine that technology has slimmed them down a bit.  Sorry, Im not a radio buff. What do they look like these days?  By the way, are you able to receive police/fire transmission as high as 800mhz with a ham?  He definitely has a scanner or a ham if its possible to get as high as 800 with a ham.  Then again WPD probably was&#39;nt on 800mhz in that day and age. VHF I guess.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3052-->
<!--Post: 3059--><!--Time: 1104396855-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3059"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Glad<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Glad<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 12:54 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->IQ <BR> <BR>Thanks for posting that link to Ham operators in Wichita.  I don&#39;t know if it is me or just late tonight, but alot of them looked way too serious.  There were a couple of happy fellows in there but I see several possibilities based upon the eyes...would like to see more research on a few of them.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3059-->
<!--Post: 3086--><!--Time: 1104441955-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3086"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Gavinelias<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Gavinelias<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 1:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->My neighbor had a ham radio tower in his backyard until he moved.  It is not something you could miss.  Do a Google search under images for ham tower for a good idea of what they look like and the size differences between types.  Take care. <BR>Gavin<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3086-->
<!--Post: 3529--><!--Time: 1104978178-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3529"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:jsk@jvlnet.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, January 05, 2005 - 6:22 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Im guessing that he was able to listen to the police at some point in time. Id think that the WPD was on either VHF HI or LOW at that time. The 800MHz radios werent being used by many people at that time. Its also easy to hide an HF antenna if its merely a straight wire...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
